# - Homonym warning, verified on the same opened pages: the Qobuz and Viberate pages headed YSN also carry an American rapper of the same name (MG2X, Stunna 2X and Toe 2 Toe on Muzik Junky; OTA feat. Euro Gotit & YFN Lucci and WORKIN feat. Young Dolph on Authentic Empire Music Group, December 2020), and the Viberate text itself describes a Columbus, Ohio artist on the conflated page. Those United States records are NOT credited to the French West Indies beatmaker in any source opened, and this profile excludes them. YSN Flow is a third, different artist again.
# - Deezer, Rachelle Allison listings (search results, 2026-10-20): PKM, released January 17, 2025 by Mimesis, duration 2:31, composers Mike Saint-Auret, Nicolas Lanclume (YSN), Rachelle Paturot and Yohan Corneille Lanclas; Pare Ba-Y, released August 11, 2025 by Mimesis, composer Ysn; Nyet (2026), composers Rachelle Allison, Aknose and Ysn. The Deezer credit Nicolas Lanclume (YSN) is the explicit identity link between the stage name and the credit name.
# - Shazam listings (opened 2026-10-20): Vire by LULOS & YSN, released June 22, 2025 by Hakuna Music Company, 100 BPM, language French, credits YSN as Performer and Composer, Nicolas Lanclume as Songwriter; BBL by Waysee & YSN, released August 21, 2024 by Hakuna Music Company, 117 BPM, language French, songwriters Nicolas Lanclume and Yohan corneille; HOLIDAY by Krys, credits YSN as Vocals and Producer, Nicolas Lanclume as Songwriter, 130 BPM (Shazam dates this listing June 27, 2025 while Qobuz dates the Krys single February 28, 2025 on Step Out Productions: this profile keeps the year 2025 and reports the disagreement); Bad by Sanchii & YSN, released December 12, 2025 by Hakuna Music Company, language French, credits YSN as Producer and Nicolas Lanclume as Songwriter.
# - Qobuz, Krys discography (search results, 2026-10-20): GOD BLESS (Ah la vie qu'on mene) by Krys, released June 28, 2024 by KRYSmusics; the title is published as Krys feat. YSN (letras.com title and podcast tracklists). Viberate, YSN top songs (opened via search, 2026-10-20): GOD BLESS first, then Manawa, Palabras and Pran On Pye; Viberate also reports Pran On Pye as a collaboration with 1T1 and LeJuh.
# - YouTube, Aknose & YSN, Palabras, official clip page (opened 2026-10-20): after Manawa, a new title in the Dembow style; composer YSN; mix and mastering Zweeng; clip credits list the social handles of YSN as Instagram /nicolasysn, Snapchat nicolas_ysn, TikTok /ni.ysn, X Nicolasysn and YouTube channel @ysnmakeitmove; the lyrics intro carries the shout YSN MAKE THEM MOVE, and the hashtags include YSNMAKETHEMMOVE, YSNMAKEITMOVE and GUADELOUPE; P 2025 Hakuna Music Company and MBI Family. YouTube, Manawa by Aknose & YSN (search result, 2026-10-20): provided by TuneCore, P 2024 Hakuna Music Company, released September 6, 2024.
